---
// Getting around without a car (#599) and "which bus gets me to X" (#61).
// Every fact is in a resource record in content/resources/, read on
// Mountain Line's own pages (busride.org) on 2026-10-30. Left off on purpose:
// PRT hours and how many Grey Line trips run a day (sources differ, see #598),
// and a bus for the DoHS office, Health Right and food pantries (no Mountain
// Line route page names a stop at them).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import { loadDir } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { fixFormUrl } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
export const page = { door: "living-here", topic: "moving", label: "Getting around without a car", summary: "Mountain Line buses, fares, WVU Ride Free, the Grey Line to Pittsburgh, and which bus goes to the hospitals" };
const all = loadDir('resources');
const r = (slug) => all.find((e) => e.slug === slug);
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="Getting around Morgantown without a car: Mountain Line buses" description="Ride Mountain Line buses in Morgantown and Mon County: fares and passes, free rides with a WVU ID, the Grey Line, and buses to the hospitals.">
  <h1>Getting around without a car</h1>
  <p class="lede">Mountain Line runs the public buses in Morgantown and Mon County. Most local buses stop anywhere along the route if you wave to the driver. For live bus times, use Mountain Line's <a href="https://www.busride.org/google-trip-planner">trip planner</a> or call <a href="tel:3042917433">304-291-RIDE (304-291-7433)</a>.</p>
  <p>See how it could go: <a href={`${base}/getting-around/example/`}>an example first week without a car</a> (a made-up person, real routes).</p>

  <nav aria-label="On this page">
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${base}/bus-routes/`}>Every bus route and when it runs</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${base}/bus-passes/`}>Half-fare and property tax bus passes</a></li>
      <li><a href="#fares">Fares and how to ride</a></li>
      <li><a href="#wvu">Free with a WVU ID</a></li>
      <li><a href="#which-bus">Which bus gets me to the hospital?</a></li>
      <li><a href="#pittsburgh">Bus to Pittsburgh and the airport</a></li>
      <li><a href="#rides">Can't take the bus to a medical visit?</a></li>
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="fares">Fares and how to ride</h2>
  {r('mountain-line-fares') && <ResourceCard r={r('mountain-line-fares')} showCost />}

  <h2 id="wvu">Free with a WVU ID</h2>
  {r('mountain-line-wvu-ride-free') && <ResourceCard r={r('mountain-line-wvu-ride-free')} />}

  <h2 id="which-bus">Which bus gets me to the hospital?</h2>
  <p>First and last runs are when the route starts its first and last trip. The bus reaches your stop later, so check the trip planner for the time at your stop.</p>
  {r('bus-to-ruby-memorial') && <ResourceCard r={r('bus-to-ruby-memorial')} />}
  {r('bus-to-mon-general') && <ResourceCard r={r('bus-to-mon-general')} />}
  <p>Going somewhere else, like the Department of Human Services (DoHS) office, the Health Right clinic or a food pantry? Mountain Line's route pages do not name a stop at those places, so we have not listed a bus for them. Type the address into the <a href="https://www.busride.org/google-trip-planner">trip planner</a>, or call 304-291-RIDE and ask.</p>

  <h2 id="pittsburgh">Bus to Pittsburgh and the airport</h2>
  {r('grey-line-pittsburgh') && <ResourceCard r={r('grey-line-pittsburgh')} showCost />}

  <p>Driving instead? See <a href={`${base}/parking/`}>Parking in Morgantown</a> for garage and meter rates and what to do about a ticket.</p>

  <h2 id="rides">Can't take the bus to a medical visit?</h2>
  {r('mountain-line-newfit') && <ResourceCard r={r('mountain-line-newfit')} showCost />}
  <p>On Medicaid or WVCHIP? See <a href={`${base}/medical-rides/`}>Ride to a medical visit</a> for rides through Modivcare.</p>

  <p class="meta">Sources checked October 30, 2026. Routes and times change, so check the trip planner before you go. Hours for the WVU PRT (Personal Rapid Transit) are not on this page yet because we could not confirm them on WVU's page. Something out of date? <a href={fixFormUrl({ page: Astro.url.pathname })}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
